o pursue that we're not gonna let  russia dictate  in any way what's in our interests and  how to pursue them  media ukraine um just a few days ago  european union proposed to donate their  fighter jets to ukraine to protect our  sky but as far as they know for now this  deal has fallen apart i know that you  were in a phone call with foreign  minister coleman today discussing with  this topic as well could one expect that  after after your travel to europe  something could change and ukraine will  get access to those jets  thank you um i  i can't comment in detail in my  conversations with foreign minister  khalifa we uh we talked about a lot of  things including  uh the ongoing provision of security  assistance to uh to ukraine uh and that  is something that i will be talking to  european allies and uh and partners  about in a couple of days in in brussels  uh again i can tell you is  um i mentioned in response to andrea's  question that when it comes to vital uh  defensive military equipment uh that uh  that ukraine needs uh we are very uh  actively coordinating its provision and  that assistance is uh is getting there  but we'll probably have more to say in  the next couple of days thank you thank  you very much thanks everyone thank you  very much  sir do you think that russia is  deliberately targeting civilians you  said they're hitting schools and  hospitals  are they doing it deliberately  we've certainly seen uh in the past that  um  one of russia's methods of war  uh is  to be absolutely brutal  in trying to  cow the citizenry  uh of um of a given country  and that includes  at the very least  indiscriminate  targeting  and potentially deliberate targeting as  well  we're looking very closely at uh what's  happening in ukraine right now  including what's happening to uh to  civilians  uh we're taking account of it  we're documenting it  and we want to ensure among other things  that there's accountability for it  thank you thank you mr secretary  you
 

